{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04T8", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-fibre-products}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dbd872c2a449cd66d1e295d8db4d257c7369da790abe89d9f393ae7e2589d62d", "source_text": "Fibre products of algebraic spaces", "source_text_hash": "sha256:383afbcabcaaf0da2792cacb67e85fed272e017b6c3b50dafe246c4bc9e1007d", "unit_id": "tag:04T8:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04T8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:86ec2eecd570d0c8a4f479624baf284069e51967c1f2fc353abd21054aea9915", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e4e8e8f4e0931a3bb4cf0b8ce8528cab89790f9f5d448ad7d8cb2ae6ec056438", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe category of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0001> has both products and\nfibre products.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:61a1d80920fc3ba299961c860dff996c208eb6911ba317c199da9eda936afb55", "unit_id": "tag:04T8:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04T8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$F, G$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$F \\times G$", "MATH_0006": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-product-spaces}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:13e3ea3010ef00c498e5e8456be47abc02b4d2eb0f25a88840ca7380db57eec9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:319ceec925087f133fbc33f5c9dc07331e7a2d0a61481923601acfe51069035f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be algebraic spaces over <MATH_0004>.\nThen <MATH_0005> is an algebraic space, and is a product\nin the category of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2a62d9051de27b8b774b6528c4bfd146be47d1c897d8797345f4cdc39af44851", "unit_id": "tag:02X0:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04T8", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$H = F \\times G$", "MATH_0002": "$H$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$G$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to F$", "MATH_0006": "$V \\to G$", "MATH_0007": "$U, V \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\times V \\to F \\times G$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-product-representable-transformations}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-product-representable-transformations-property}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a2400c9bcf0626cc74c6eee38e3092a3088fa1a070aa20837d106a6302d48aa4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3c6f15fec7617bb00039cd22e5a442e41ef2e1528335c8e5f1e9be10ca95b093", "source_text": "It is clear that <MATH_0001> is a sheaf.\nThe diagonal of <MATH_0002> is simply the product of the\ndiagonals of <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004>. Hence it is representable by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nFinally, if <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are surjective\n<ACCENT_0001>tale morphisms, with <MATH_0007>,\nthen <MATH_0008> is surjective <ACCENT_0002>tale\nby Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1432d1d28e181023f29550728ec1fc51141863c45efb3b7b29c49bf187d58eda", "unit_id": "tag:02X0:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04T8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$H$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$F, G$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$F \\to H$", "MATH_0008": "$G \\to H$", "MATH_0009": "$F \\times_H G$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fibre-product-spaces-over-sheaf-with-representable-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:438ef29e13d2a89a18d206fe4b90d267317996c994fd7faaaa8124585506b59f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2288e8f06e0a7a60174e00fe8d2e80403ae9655a69d1d7738c8e570f78cb3717", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a sheaf on <MATH_0004> whose diagonal\nis representable. Let <MATH_0005> be algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>.\nLet <MATH_0007>, <MATH_0008> be maps of sheaves.\nThen <MATH_0009> is an algebraic space.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:75b9f3d687833a373d809f3269ec3f16d906fb4173f46aafba143c3bf3814868", "unit_id": "tag:04T9:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04T8", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$F \\times_H G$", "MATH_0002": "$F \\times_H G$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nF \\times_H G \\ar[r] \\ar[d]_\\Delta &\nF \\times G \\ar[d]^{\\Delta_F \\times \\Delta_G} \\\\\n(F \\times F) \\times_{(H \\times H)} (G \\times G) \\ar[r] &\n(F \\times F) \\times (G \\times G)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0005": "$U, V \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0006": "$a : U \\to F$", "MATH_0007": "$b : V \\to G$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta_H$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\times_H V$", "MATH_0010": "$$\nU \\times_H V \\longrightarrow F \\times_H G\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$U \\times_H V \\to U \\times_H G$", "MATH_0012": "$U \\times_H G \\to F \\times_H G$", "MATH_0013": "$U \\to F$", "MATH_0014": "$V \\to G$", "MATH_0015": "$F \\times_H G$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-algebraic-space}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-product-representable-transformations}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-representable-transformations}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-composition-representable-transformations}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-representable-transformations}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{definition-algebraic-space}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:17bfbf3bdcdd22e6a4341043775bef21605b3cde5e3739cdb1f86b1abfbf94b8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d01480bd7e8ba69360537157f071df6b5112a51b0af9b2da0cf3105278aa6a2b", "source_text": "We check the 3 conditions of\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\nA fibre product of sheaves is a sheaf, hence <MATH_0001> is a sheaf.\nThe diagonal of <MATH_0002> is the left vertical arrow in\n<MATH_0003>\nwhich is cartesian. Hence <MATH_0004> is representable as the base change\nof the morphism on the right which is representable, see\nLemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\nFinally, let <MATH_0005>\nand <MATH_0006>, <MATH_0007> be surjective and <ACCENT_0001>tale.\nAs <MATH_0008> is representable, we see that <MATH_0009> is a scheme.\nThe morphism\n<MATH_0010>\nis surjective and <ACCENT_0002>tale as a composition of the base changes\n<MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012>\nof the <ACCENT_0003>tale surjective morphisms <MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014>, see\nLemmas <REF_0004> and\n<REF_0005>.\nThis proves the last condition of\nDefinition <REF_0006>\nholds and we conclude that <MATH_0015> is an algebraic space.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d5c376b8e1717b87d8b0d5d5ba87fb0a92b3d1bf95bb426221944ccf6c816176", "unit_id": "tag:04T9:proof"}
